## Why This Is Asked

Tests lifecycle management, reproducibility, and safe feature releases in a privacy-conscious SageMaker setup.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Experiments and Model Registry
- Canary deployments and rollback strategies
- Drift and quality monitoring with lightweight checks
- PrivateLink isolation and VPC security

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: create an Experiment and a Trial
import { SageMakerClient, CreateExperimentCommand, CreateTrialCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker";
const c = new SageMakerClient({region: 'us-east-1'});
async function init() {
  const exp = await c.send(new CreateExperimentCommand({ExperimentName: 'TextClassifier_V1'}));
  await c.send(new CreateTrialCommand({TrialName: 'V1_Run', ExperimentName: exp.ExperimentArn}));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you automate canary rollback if latency exceeds threshold for 3 consecutive windows?
- What minimal drift signals would trigger a new model version in the registry?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect per-tenant, private data path while supporting burst workloads, with per-tenant model versions, canary rollouts, and drift monitoring in AWS ML services.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint
- PrivateLink data residency
- Per-tenant Model Registry tags
- Canary rollouts and tenant routing
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo AWS SDK calls to register and route per-tenant models
const sm = new SageMaker({region: 'us-east-1'});
sm.registerModel({ModelName:'tenantA-v2', ...});
sm.createEndpoint({EndpointName:'multi-tenant-endpoint', ...});

// Lambda routing logic
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenant = event.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const modelName = `${tenant}-latest`;
  return await sm.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: 'multi-tenant-endpoint',
    TargetModel: modelName,
    Body: JSON.stringify(event.body)
  });
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant inference, per-tenant SLAs, and practical routing inside an MME while keeping data in a VPC.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint and on-demand loading
- Per-tenant routing and model versioning
- Auto Scaling and canary rollouts by tenant
- Drift detection, validation, data residency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: per-request routing to specific model on an MME
const { SageMakerRuntimeClient, InvokeEndpointCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker-runtime");
const client = new SageMakerRuntimeClient({region:'us-east-1'});
async function infer(endpoint, modelName, payload){
  return await client.send(new InvokeEndpointCommand({
    EndpointName: endpoint,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Accept: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify({ instances: [payload], modelName })
  }));
}
``

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate explainability, bias auditing, drift monitoring, and controlled deployment in a multi-tenant, VPC-isolated AWS environment.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Clarify for bias and explainability
- Model Monitor drift detection
- PrivateLink and private feature store integration
- Canary rollout with per-tenant isolation
- Auditable logging to S3

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing snippet for multi-tenant endpoint
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const endpoint = `rt-endpoint-${tenant}`;
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, req.body);
}
```

